From: "lich.wang" <lich.wang@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:07:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Input: touchscreen: add the Novatek NT36532 SPI vendor driver

Touch and active pen (Lenovo Tab Pen Plus: pressure, tilt, two buttons)
of the Lenovo Xiaoxin Pad Pro GT (TB710FU).  This is Novatek's driver
as ported by SpendyYT and MeteoricmeteorLL/tb710fu-linux; the firmware
is loaded with request_firmware().

It matches "novatek,nt36532-ts-spi" only: "novatek,NVT-ts-spi" is
already claimed by the NT36536 driver (nt36536_ts).  It builds as a
module only, since the vendor sources share global symbol names with
that driver.

Fixes on top of the vendor code:
- /proc/NVTSPI: bound the user-supplied transfer length by the request
  and by the SPI read buffer, and make the node root-only;
- bound the /proc/edge_grid_zone and /proc/Pen_ID writes;
- release single_open() proc files with single_release(), give
  fw_pen_state its read/release ops, and stop making game_mode and
  support_pen world-writable;
- drop the Android-only "novatek_ts" platform device, which was
  unregistered up to three times;
- change the pen pressure range in place instead of freeing the
  registered input device;
- on remove, stop the charger and restore-command work and free the
  read buffer; unwind module init on failure; no hard-coded legacy GPIO;
- run the FW health check under ts->lock and stop it across system
  suspend.
